<section | Top-level bare pipe table>

A bare GFM pipe table in top-level prose, normalized to a canonical table node:

| Symbol | Meaning  |
| ------ | -------- |
| F      | Force    |
| m      | Mass     |
| a      | Acceleration |

<section | Aligned columns>

A table with explicit column alignment:

| Left | Right | Center | Default |
| :--- | ---: | :---: | --- |
| A    | B    | C      | D       |
| 1    | 2    | 3      | 4       |

<section #sec:markup-cells | Inline markup in cells>

Bare GFM pipe-table body cells preserve inline markup — emphasis, inline code, and
inline math — instead of flattening to plain text (#280). A cross-reference in a cell
resolves like any other (the carried cell mdast is reached by the resolution passes):

| Construct   | Example                     |
| ----------- | --------------------------- |
| Emphasis    | *stressed* and **strong**   |
| Inline code | `f(x)`                      |
| Inline math | $E = mc^2$                  |
| Reference   | see <ref @sec:markup-cells> |

Header markup, by contrast, is flattened (the headers model is text-only):

| *Header markup is dropped* | Plain header |
| -------------------------- | ------------ |
| body                       | cells        |

<section | Table inside named-tag content>

A bare pipe table inside a named tag's pipe-content (inner processor path):

